{
  "hypothesis": "The October 13 redefinition of the session-start event, which decides whether a new user counts as having opened the app the next day, is counting fewer real day-1 returns, so the drop from 38% to 31% is a measurement artifact rather than a real change in user behavior.",
  "check": "Recompute Day-1 retention for every daily install cohort from the six weeks before October 13 through today using one consistent session-start definition (apply the new definition to the pre-October-13 raw app-open events, or the old definition to the post-October-13 events); if the October 13 step disappears and the series stays flat, the redefinition is confirmed as the cause, and if the roughly 7-point drop remains under a consistent definition, it is ruled out."
}

